      {
        "id": "p57-q7",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $f$ be an even function with domain that includes $x=a$. If $f$ is increasing at $x=a$, then $f$ is decreasing at $x=-a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True. For even $f$, $f'(-a)=-f'(a)<0$.",
          "worked": "Since $f$ is even, $f'(-a)=-f'(a)$. As $f'(a)>0$, we have $f'(-a)<0$, so $f$ is decreasing at $x=-a$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q8",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Let $f$ be an even function with domain that includes $x=a$. If $f$ is increasing at $x=a$, then $f$ is increasing at $x=-a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. For even $f$, $f'(-a)=-f'(a)<0$.",
          "worked": "Since $f$ is even, $f'(-a)=-f'(a)$. As $f'(a)>0$, we have $f'(-a)<0$, so $f$ is decreasing at $x=-a$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q9",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Let $f$ be an odd function with domain that includes $x=a$. If $f$ is increasing at $x=a$, then $f$ is decreasing at $x=-a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. For odd $f$, $f'(-a)=f'(a)>0$.",
          "worked": "Since $f$ is odd, $f'(-a)=f'(a)$. As $f'(a)>0$, we have $f'(-a)>0$, so $f$ is increasing at $x=-a$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
